 "about": "The table of examples of what a send puts on the pass and what it holds back, and of what « order the next course » releases (NeoRestau lot 1, service families). The server (pos_next/restaurant/service_families.py: plan_send, next_release, held_lines) and the till (POS/src/utils/serviceFamilies.js: planKitchenSend, nextRelease, heldLines) are each tested against THIS file, so that the lines the dialog ticks and the lines the server sends cannot drift apart. A line is {service_family, kds_status}: the status is empty for a line not sent yet, Waiting for a held line, anything else for a line that has left. send_cases: `plan` is one of send / hold / left per line, `sent_families` the families of the lines the stored order already sent. next_cases: `next` is the family and the indexes of the lines released by « the next course », `all` the indexes of every held line (« order everything »).",
